# VARUNA Hybrid TransUNet — Deep Architecture Explainer

> A deep-dive into how VARUNA reads atmospheric data across **space**, **time**, and **multiple disaster types** simultaneously.

---

## The Core Problem VARUNA Solves

Traditional weather models treat every pixel of a weather map independently. They fail to answer three fundamental questions at once:

| Question | Challenge | VARUNA's Solution |
|---|---|---|
| **When?** | Weather is a movie, not a photo | 3D Convolutional Temporal Compression |
| **Where?** | Fine-grained spatial precision needed | 2D U-Net encoder/decoder with skip connections |
| **What's related?** | Arabian Sea moisture → Himalayan storm | Multi-Head Self-Attention at the bottleneck |
| **Which disaster?** | Cloudburst ≠ Thunderstorm ≠ Flash Flood | 3 independent multi-task decoder heads |

VARUNA handles all four simultaneously in a single forward pass.

